def SRC := /opt/data/workspace/hermes-context/ (canonical host mount, read-only)
def DST := /workspace/hermes-context/ (user workspace, rsync --delete mirror)
def LOG := outside DST always, ~/.cache default; entrypoints := ~/.local/bin or /workspace/hdcs/bin, never inside DST
A1_placement: SRC host -> DST workspace, one-way; nothing writes back to host mount
A2_units: systemd USER units (systemctl --user), timer every 6h; script must work standalone sans systemd
A3_fallback: rsync absent -> cp -a + recursive reconcile; both paths converge identically
A4_contents: sync CONTENTS of SRC into DST (src/ -> dst/), never nest
A5_mirror: ∀ path -> DST end state == SRC end state, recursive; stale files/subtrees DELETED at every depth
A6_dryrun: --dry-run -> ZERO writes ∀ kind (incl. log files); DST byte-identical post-dry-run
A9_equiv_class: mirror := contents + recursive structure + symlinks (levels 1-3); NOT metadata/timestamps/hardlinks; self-verify FAILs nonzero on mismatch, never warn-and-exit-0
A10_severity: FAIL only on defects reachable in normal operation / plausible destructive misconfig; adversarial env algebra -> +open KNOWN_LIMITATIONS, non-blocking
A11_source_survival: guard SRC==DST; never rm -rf DST before verified copy of SRC exists elsewhere
A12_identity: compare realpath(SRC) vs realpath(DST); refuse on identity, ancestor/descendant, or symlink-into-SRC; both paths, before any destructive op
A13_verified: stage -> content-compare (A9 class) -> only then touch DST; non-emptiness ≠ verification; script exits nonzero on staging verify fail
A14_protected: refuse (clean nonzero, no writes) iff realpath(DST) ==/contains script-owned CONCRETE paths (stage dir, log file parent, entrypoint dir); stage must not resolve inside DST/SRC (TMPDIR included); beyond this guard, env combos = KNOWN_LIMITATIONS
A15_calibration: owned := concrete instantiated path (mktemp -d result, resolved log parent, resolved entrypoint dir), never generic ancestors; refuse iff boundary-aware containment (component split), never string-prefix; over-broad wall = defect
validation: [dry-run byte-identity, mirror equivalence A9, destructive-op ordering A11-A13, A14 gate calibration]
open: [newline-in-filename corpora; exotic env combos beyond A14 guard — KNOWN_LIMITATIONS, non-blocking]
